 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For each of the following compound logical statements, add parentheses to indicate the order in which to evaluate the statement. Recall that parentheses are evaluated innermost first.\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 496967,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"p \\vee q \\wedge \\text{~}r\">p \\vee q \\wedge \\text{~}r</span>\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"((p \\vee q) \\wedge (\\text{~}r))\">((p \\vee q) \\wedge (\\text{~}r))</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The order of logical operations is</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Parentheses</li>\n<li>Negation</li>\n<li>Disjunction, conjunction</li>\n<li>Conditional</li>\n<li>Biconditional</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For same order operations, work left to right.</p>\n<p>The highest order operation in this expression is negation, so add parentheses around the negation.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p \\vee q\\; \\wedge \\left( {{\\text{~}}r} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Disjunction and conjunction are the same order, so work left to right. First evaluate the exclusive or.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(p \\vee q) \\wedge \\left( {{\\text{~}}r} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Then finish by evaluating the conjunction.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"((p \\vee q) \\wedge \\left( {{\\text{~}}r} \\right))\"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 496968,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{~}p \\to q \\vee r\">\\text{~} p \\to q \\vee r</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"((\\text{~}p) \\to (q \\vee r))\">((\\text{~}p) \\to (q \\vee r))</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The order of logical operations is</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Parentheses</li>\n<li>Negation</li>\n<li>Disjunction, conjunction</li>\n<li>Conditional</li>\n<li>Biconditional</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For same order operations, work left to right.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}p{\\text{ }} \\to {\\text{ }}q \\vee r\"></span></p>\n<p>The highest order operation in this expression is negation, so add parentheses around the negation.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {{\\text{~}}p} \\right) \\to {\\text{ }}q \\vee r\"></span></p>\n<p>The next highest order operation is the disjunction. Add parentheses around the disjunction.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {{\\text{~}}p} \\right) \\to (q \\vee r)\"></span></p>\n<p>Finally, you can evaluate the conditional.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(\\left( {{\\text{~}}p} \\right) \\to (q \\vee r))\"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 496969,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{~}p \\vee \\text{~}q\\, \\leftrightarrow \\,\\text{~}(p \\wedge q)\">\\text{~}p \\vee \\text{~}q\\, \\leftrightarrow \\,\\text{~}(p \\wedge q)</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"((\\text{~}p) \\vee (\\text{~}q)) \\leftrightarrow (\\text{~}(p \\wedge q))\">((\\text{~}p) \\vee (\\text{~}q)) \\leftrightarrow (\\text{~}(p \\wedge q))</span>; this is another example of De Morgan’s Laws and it is always true."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The order of logical operations is</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Parentheses</li>\n<li>Negation</li>\n<li>Disjunction, conjunction</li>\n<li>Conditional</li>\n<li>Biconditional</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For same order operations, work left to right.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{~}}p \\vee {\\text{~}}q{\\text{ }} \\leftrightarrow {\\text{~}}(p \\wedge q)\"></span></p>\n<p>The right side of the biconditional already has parentheses. The next step in the order of operation is negation, so add parentheses around the three negations.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {{\\text{~}}p} \\right) \\vee ({\\text{~}}q) \\leftrightarrow ({\\text{~}}(p \\wedge q))\"></span></p>\n<p>The next step in the order of operations is disjunction/conjunction. Add parentheses around the disjunction.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(\\left( {{\\text{~}}p} \\right) \\vee ({\\text{~}}q)) \\leftrightarrow ({\\text{~}}(p \\wedge q))\"></span></p>\n<p>The lowest order operation is the biconditional. Finish by evaluating the biconditional.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"((\\left( {{\\text{~}}p} \\right) \\vee ({\\text{~}}q)) \\leftrightarrow ({\\text{~}}(p \\wedge q)))\"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
